 34CL    32S(A,D)                      1982DE29,1977NA10,1976DE24ENSDF    202609
 34CL  H TYP=FUL$AUT=LIJIE SUN AND JUN CHEN$CIT=ENSDF$CUT=30-Sep-2026$          
 34CL  H TYP=FUL$AUT=NINEL NICA, BALRAJ SINGH$CIT=NDS 113, 1563 (2012)$         
 34CL2 H CUT=28-May-2012$                                                       
 34CL c  {+32}S+1p+1n|){+34}Cl from J|p=0+ {+32}S ground state.                 
 34CL c  1982De29,1981De37: a 50-MeV |a beam was produced from the KVI          
 34CL2c  cyclotron. Targets were solid S evaporated onto C foil and covered with
 34CL3c  a C layer and gaseous H{-2}S. Reaction products were detected using a  
 34CL4c  Si |DE-E telescope. Measured |s(E{-d},|q). Deduced levels, L-transfers,
 34CL5c  J, |p, and spectroscopic factors from zero-range DWUCK-DWBA analysis.  
 34CL c  1977Na10: a 40-MeV |a beam was produced from the Michigan State        
 34CL2c  University cyclotron. Targets were 99.9%-enriched {+32}S of 110        
 34CL3c  |mg/cm{+2} sandwiched between layers of Formvar and carbon foils.      
 34CL4c  Reaction products were detected in the focal plane of an Enge          
 34CL5c  split-pole magnetic spectrograph with a proportional-counter           
 34CL6c  plastic-scintillator combination with FWHM=40-60 keV. Measured         
 34CL7c  |s(E{-d},|q). Deduced levels, J, |p, and L-transfers.                  
 34CL c  1976De24: a 40-MeV |a beam was produced from the Princeton azimuthally 
 34CL2c  varying field cyclotron. The target was CdS with natural {+32}S.       
 34CL3c  Reaction products were detected using a freon cooled |DE-E Si detector 
 34CL4c  telescope with FWHM=50 keV. Measured |s(E{-d},|q). Deduced levels,     
 34CL5c  L-transfers, J, and |p from DWUCK-DWBA analysis. Also measured         
 34CL6c  {+32}S({+3}He,p){+34}Cl.                                               
 34CL c  1966Ki10: a 29.0-MeV |a beam was produced from the 105-cm Kyoto        
 34CL2c  University cyclotron. Targets were 0.78-mg/cm{+2}-thick sulfur covered 
 34CL3c  by thick gold foils. Reaction products were detected using a 50-|mm |DE
 34CL4c  surface barrier and 5-mm E lithium drifted detectors. Deduced levels,  
 34CL5c  L-transfers, J, and |p from DWBA analysis.                             
 34CL cL E,L$From 1982De29, unless otherwise noted.                             
 34CL cL E(K)$From 1966Ki10.                                                    
